{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MassTowerDeeperFillers","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MassTowerDeeperFillers","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.MassTowerOpenProblemsClasses","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.TypeBFoldedCrystalCombinatorics","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.ClausenFunctionMathlibFiller","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerMathlibFiller","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.BlochWignerLobachevsky","lean:module:QOU.Knot.CatalanValueBounds"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.not_deeperMathlibFillers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.not_deeperMathlibFillers","kind":"theorem","line":184,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L184-L189","doc":"Consequently `DeeperMathlibFillers F` has no instance for any `F`, and\nevery theorem with a `[DeeperMathlibFillers F]` hypothesis (here\n`Cl_2_zero_consistent_with_pentagon`) is vacuously true, not evidence\nthat the fillers are consistent. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.not_cl_2_pentagonIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.not_cl_2_pentagonIdentity","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L164-L182","doc":"**`Cl_2_PentagonIdentity` is FALSE, so the class has no instance.**\n\nIts field quantifies over *all* `α β γ : ℝ`.  At `α = π/2`, `β = γ = 0`\nthe five terms are `Cl₂(π/2) − 0 + Cl₂(−π/2) − Cl₂(π/2) + 0 = Cl₂(−π/2)`,\nand `Cl₂(−π/2) = −Cl₂(π/2) = −G < 0` (oddness, `Cl_2_neg`; positivity of\nCatalan's constant, `Cl_2_pi_div_two_pos`).  The genuine five-term\nrelation holds only on the pentagon closure locus, which the field omits\n(compare `Cl_2_PentagonHolds.closure` in\n`QOU.Archimedean.ThreeSubstantiveMathlibFillers`).\n\nRecorded 2026-11-15 (bean `qou-6qbv`).  The class is left as it stands:\nrestating it is a change to the remark's content and waits for the owner. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_zero_consistent_with_pentagon","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_zero_consistent_with_pentagon","kind":"theorem","line":154,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L154-L162","doc":"**Conditional theorem: with the deeper fillers, `Cl_2(0) = 0`\nis consistent with pentagon identity at the trivial point.**\n\nTrivial — `Cl_2(0) = 0` already proved unconditionally — but\nserves as a sanity-check that the deeper-filler typeclass is\nnon-trivially inhabitable in the trivial case. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.DeeperMathlibFillers.pentagon_identity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.DeeperMathlibFillers.pentagon_identity","kind":"theorem","line":152,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L152-L152","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.DeeperMathlibFillers.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.DeeperMathlibFillers.mk","kind":"ctor","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L150-L150","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.DeeperMathlibFillers","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.DeeperMathlibFillers","kind":"class","line":144,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L144-L152","doc":"**Synthesis: assembled deeper-filler typeclass.**\n\nA type carrying all deeper-filler instances simultaneously.\nInhabiting this class collects (E) — the three\nMathlib-pending structural hypotheses — and is the natural\nnext §3b-cond hook for full BlochSuslinUniqueness closure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_PentagonIdentity.pentagon_holds_modulo_2pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_PentagonIdentity.pentagon_holds_modulo_2pi","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L140-L140","doc":"The 5-term pentagon, restricted to the unit-circle `Cl_2` form:\nfor arguments `α, β, γ` in the standard fundamental domain the\nalternating five-term sum vanishes.  Encoding the genuine\nfunctional equation (not a `True` placeholder); an instance is the\nconjectural input pending Mathlib's `Real.sin` / Fourier-series\n`tsum` identities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_PentagonIdentity.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_PentagonIdentity.mk","kind":"ctor","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L133-L133","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_PentagonIdentity","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.Cl_2_PentagonIdentity","kind":"class","line":121,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L121-L142","doc":"The **5-term pentagon identity** for the Bloch-Wigner\ndilogarithm restricted to the unit circle (`Cl_2` form):\n\n  Cl_2(α) - Cl_2(β) + Cl_2(β - α)\n    - Cl_2(α - γ) + Cl_2(β - γ)  =  0     (modulo 2π).\n\nThis is the trigonometric form of the standard pentagon, valid\nwhen all five arguments lie in the standard fundamental domain.\nFull proof needs Mathlib's `Real.sin` / Fourier-series\nidentities at the `tsum` level. We axiomatise it as a\ntypeclass with a single field. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.KLClassicalLimit_const","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.KLClassicalLimit_const","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L100-L103","doc":"Trivial property of the classical-limit functor: applied to\na constant, returns the constant. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.KLClassicalLimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.KLClassicalLimit","kind":"def","line":85,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L85-L98","doc":"The **classical-limit specialisation** sends a Hecke trace over the\nground ring `R`, at substrate parameter `q`, to its `q = 1` value.\nBelow this is a placeholder; the substantive content is the\nKL-basis specialisation `b_w → C_w ∈ ℤ[S_n]` which produces\n*integer ±1 permutation signs* in the limit.\n\nGround ring generic (§7c): the `q = 1` specialisation of\n`H_n(R, q) → ℤ[S_n]` is a ring homomorphism of the Hecke ground\nring and uses no archimedean structure — no ordering, no limit, no\n`Real.*`. It was previously typed `ℝ → ℝ`, which mislabelled a\nsubstrate-side operation as archimedean; `CommRing` is the §7c\nclass for the intended instance `ℤ[q, q⁻¹]`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.heightSixPartition_finite_existence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.heightSixPartition_finite_existence","kind":"theorem","line":65,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L65-L73","doc":"The set of height-6 partitions of `n` is finite (bounded above\nby the number of compositions of `n` into 6 parts). We expose\nthis as a structural fact via Decidable infrastructure rather\nthan enumerate explicitly. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.sum_eq_n","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.sum_eq_n","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L63-L63","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.parts_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.parts_pos","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L62-L62","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.height_eq_six","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.height_eq_six","kind":"theorem","line":61,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L61-L61","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.parts","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.parts","kind":"def","line":60,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L60-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L59-L59","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.DeeperFillers.HeightSixPartition","kind":"structure","line":54,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-tower-deeper-fillers.lean#L54-L63","doc":"A partition of `n` represented as a non-increasing list of\npositive parts, with **height** = number of parts. We restrict\nto partitions of height exactly 6 — the level-5 GS-filtration\ndiagnostic from `conj:shell-correction-term-seven`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}